<content:encoded><![CDATA[<p><i>Sponsored by <strong>Gamut Podcast Network</strong>. Want top 10 network reach and a team that actually emails you back? Gamut does both. If your show should be making more money, let’s talk. Email dan@gamutpodcasts.com or <a class="l" style="font-weight:bold;color:#BC1515" href="https://podnews.net/class-click/3849/2026-11-24">visit Gamut Podcast Network</a></i></p><ul>
<li><a href="https://podnews.net/press-release/libsyn-monet-x-change">Libsyn has expanded its partnership with Monét X Change</a>, adding <a href="https://podnews.net/podcast/iyjwz"><cite>Monét Talks</cite></a> to its hosting and advertising roster. The show was with Studio71 US, which recently announced <a href="https://podnews.net/update/bouvard-leaves-westwood-one#story3">its closure</a>.  She already co-hosts <a href="https://podnews.net/podcast/ibm3"><cite>Sibling Rivalry</cite></a> with the company. </li>
<li><a href="https://podnews.net/press-release/edit-the-pod">Edit The Pod is a new web-based editor</a> that turns finished audio edits into video shows - grab the audio you've already mixed, give it the raw video files, and it matches it all up to produce a video version. The tool is already being used by a podcast production studio, and it can even cut a wide 4K shot into individual camera close-ups.</li>
<li>Spreaker is now sending emails when a show is imported, as per <a href="https://podnews.net/article/migration-code-of-practice">the code of practice</a> the company said it would <a href="https://podnews.net/press-release/spreaker-commitment">commit to</a> after our reporting. The code of practice has now been agreed to by a number of podcast companies.</li>
